Do not look up an absent sensor when merging same-time samples.
merge_samples() indexed the cylinder map with as->sensor[j] unchecked. A slot with
no sensor holds NO_SENSOR (-1), so it read before the start of the map, and the
value read could be written to sample.sensor[j]. sensors_renumber() checks for
this; this loop did not. Found by AddressSanitizer through a dive merge.

--- a/core/dive.cpp	2026-11-06 18:07:37
+++ b/core/dive.cpp	2026-11-06 18:07:37
@@ -1232,6 +1232,8 @@
 		for (int j = 0; j < MAX_SENSORS; ++j) {
 			int sensor_id;
 
+			if (as->sensor[j] == NO_SENSOR)
+				continue;
 			sensor_id = cylinders_map_a[as->sensor[j]];
 			if (sensor_id < 0)
 				continue;
